 {:at softland.store.gate.decision/standing
  :state :a-sessions
  :what "The word of an act for a lane of the other gate comes from the act alone: a session's rule, and no decision of Sid's. One half of the rule is forced by his line that the store comes out the same when it is run again: the word cannot follow the other gate's record, since a word that followed what the other gate had made by then would follow an order across two depots, which no second run gives again. The other half is the session's choice: which of the two words is then given, `:lane-belongs-to-the-other-gate`. `:lane-not-made` for every such act would hold his line as well."
  :source "a session, 14 October 2026"}
